From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:46:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/25] UefiPayloadPkg: Connect the disks before processing
 capsules on disk

DxeCapsuleLibFmp finds capsules on disk through the active boot option,
whose device path is usually a short-form HD() node, as efibootmgr and OS
installers create it. Before the consoles are connected that path doesn't
resolve, so the first ProcessCapsules() pass finds no capsule. The second
pass finds and removes the file, but FmpDxe has locked the firmware
device at EndOfDxe by then and the update fails.

Connect all devices before the first pass when the OS asked for capsules
on disk. This is what EDK2's PcdCapsuleOnDiskConnectBootDevice is for,
which MrChromebox's tree doesn't have. Third-party images stay deferred
until EndOfDxe, so only firmware drivers run.

Drop this, and coreboot's "payloads/external/edk2: Don't set
PcdCapsuleOnDiskConnectBootDevice", once this tree defines the PCD.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c      | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
index cdfd97bd3a..7a9d7f0794 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
@@ -477,6 +477,17 @@ PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole (
 
     BootSplashApply ();
 
+    //
+    // Capsules on disk are read from the ESP of the active boot option, which
+    // is usually a short-form HD() path that only resolves once the disks are
+    // connected. This first pass is the one that can still update the
+    // firmware: FmpDxe locks it at EndOfDxe. Third-party images (option ROMs)
+    // stay deferred until EndOfDxe, so only built-in drivers run here.
+    //
+    if (CoDCheckCapsuleOnDiskFlag ()) {
+      EfiBootManagerConnectAll ();
+    }
+
     Status = ProcessCapsules ();
     if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
       DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "%a(): ProcessCapsule() failed with: %r\n", __func__, Status));
